<title>AUSTRIA: SKIFLYING-WORLD CUP RESULTS.</title>
<headline>SKIFLYING-WORLD CUP RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>BAD MITTERNDORF, Austria 1997-02-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results from the</p>
<p>first day of the World Cup ski-flying competition on Saturday:</p>
<p>1. Takanobu Okabe (Japan) 379.9 points, (198.5/196.0 metres)</p>
<p>2. Andreas Goldberger (Austria) 368.3, (191.5/190.0)</p>
<p>3. Primoz Peterka (Slovenia) 357.5, (179.5/195.5)</p>
<p>4. Robert Meglic (Slovenia) 341.1, (183.5/177.0)</p>
<p>5. Janne Ahonen (Finland) 341.0, (177.5/182.5)</p>
<p>6. Jakub Suchacek (Czech Republic) 336.8, (173.0/183.5)</p>
<p>7. Kazuyoshi Funaki (Japan) 334.5, (181.0/171.5)</p>
<p>8. Tommy Ingebrigtsen (Norway) 332.9, (178.0/176.5)</p>
<p>9. Lasse Ottesen (Norway) 330.4, (170.5/181.5)</p>
<p>10. Akira Higashi (Japan) 329.8, (179.0/172.5)</p>
<p>World Cup standings after 18 events:</p>
<p>1. Peterka 997 points</p>
<p>2. Dieter Thoma (Germany) 984</p>
<p>3. Okabe 740</p>
<p>4. Goldberger 737</p>
<p>5. Hiroya Saito (Japan) 715</p>
<p>6. Kristian Brenden (Norway) 600</p>
<p>7. Kazuyoshi Funaki 573</p>
<p>8. Adam Malysz (Poland) 517</p>
<p>9. Ahonen 511</p>
<p>10.Janni Soininen (Finland) 458</p>
